<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Force Publique</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1885–1960</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Force Publique was the army and police force of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-free-state">Congo Free State</a> and the Belgian Congo, created in 1885–1886, with African soldiers under European officers. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-ii">Leopold II</a> it enforced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a> quotas through hostage-taking, floggings and mutilations. It fought in both world wars, and its mutiny in July 1960 opened the Congo Crisis.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/force-publique.jpg" alt="Force Publique" width="320" height="286" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Force_Publique1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
